id: pm-5iwfkj
title: "GH-1354: Linked-test snapshot mode drops nested package dependencies and breaks monorepo acceptance"
description: Published linked-test snapshot mode reportedly loses independently installed nested package dependencies.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,context-management,github-intake
created_at: "2026-09-30T06:48:35.183Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T19:46:23.956Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-02T19:46:23.822Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-02T19:46:23.822Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Real filesystem regression retains distinct root and nested dependency versions without flattening; Snapshot and ordinary linked runs preserve PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH isolation; Dependency write/isolation behavior is documented and tested; Current built and packed artifacts pass the reporter contract
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "The SDK seeds copied-source snapshots with absolute root and nested dependency junctions, preserves independent installed versions, and ignores dangling dependency links on supported filesystems."
expected_result: Linked snapshot commands resolve root and nested installed dependencies correctly and isolate tracker roots and copied-source writes.
actual_result: Six owner-linked snapshot cases and temporary npm Node/Bun monorepos pass. Revised relative-root and dangling-link controls pass. Shared full-suite receipt pm-r61juc/test-local-murdbyvj-6ohpqa passes 9608 tests with 100/100/100/100 coverage; exact observed counts are recorded in test-local-murdgisu-s8759q. Static gates and refreshed packed/dogfood consumers pass. Required hosted Windows and exact-head PR gates govern landing; publication is tracked separately by pm-7zs0.
